From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: ingenic: x1000: I2S PLL has no enable, bypass or lock bits

The I2S PLL entry left bypass_bit, enable_bit and stable_bit (s8) and
bypass_reg at zero, which the generic Ingenic PLL code reads as "bit 0" and
"register offset 0" rather than "none". Enabling the I2S clock therefore
cleared bit 0 of CPCCR, the CPU clock divider register, and polled bit 0 of
I2SCDR for lock. On the HiFi Walker H2 the first audio stream reset the
SoC instantly.

The divider is gated by the "i2s" mux (I2SCDR bits 30:29), so mark all
three as absent.

Signed-off-by: Fathom
---
diff -Naur a/drivers/clk/ingenic/x1000-cgu.c b/drivers/clk/ingenic/x1000-cgu.c
--- a/drivers/clk/ingenic/x1000-cgu.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/ingenic/x1000-cgu.c
@@ -371,6 +371,10 @@
 			.n_bits = 13,
 			.calc_m_n_od = x1000_i2spll_calc_m_n_od,
 			.set_rate_hook = x1000_i2spll_set_rate_hook,
+			/* No enable, bypass or lock bits: the "i2s" mux gates the divider */
+			.bypass_bit = -1,
+			.enable_bit = -1,
+			.stable_bit = -1,
 		},
 	},
 
